WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.211
(Music)

00:00:02.211 --> 00:00:05.005
Jennifer Aniston:
We are ripe and ready for this
conversation.

00:00:05.005 --> 00:00:07.007
And it's heartbreakingly honest.

00:00:07.007 --> 00:00:11.178
It's been one of the most
fulfilling experiences of my
life.

00:00:11.178 --> 00:00:12.179
(Music)

00:00:12.179 --> 00:00:13.764
Stand-by Eight...

00:00:13.764 --> 00:00:15.224
Eight seconds to you.

00:00:15.515 --> 00:00:20.354
The show is sharp, and
insightful, and ultimately very
human.

00:00:20.479 --> 00:00:21.480
Three...

00:00:22.022 --> 00:00:23.023
Two...

00:00:23.023 --> 00:00:24.024
Start your move...

00:00:24.858 --> 00:00:25.859
Cue her!

00:00:26.151 --> 00:00:27.402
Good morning!

00:00:27.402 --> 00:00:30.030
(Music)

00:00:30.030 --> 00:00:33.700
Our show, The Morning Show, is
really set in the world of
morning television.

00:00:33.742 --> 00:00:36.036
Janina Gavankar:
The world of the anchors, and
the news,

00:00:36.036 --> 00:00:39.122
and all of the people
that wake you up in the
mornings.

00:00:39.122 --> 00:00:43.752
There's just this adrenalized,
very ambitious, and almost
Machiavellian energy.

00:00:43.752 --> 00:00:49.341
The anxiety, fear of losing your
position, desire to come out on
top.

00:00:49.341 --> 00:00:51.551
This shows me what this world
is.

00:00:51.551 --> 00:00:57.808
Mitch and Alex are the darlings
of morning tv. They're
incredibly close friends.

00:00:57.808 --> 00:00:59.268
And there's a love between them.

00:00:59.309 --> 00:01:02.187
Mitch, that's my on-air partner.
My tv husband.

00:01:02.187 --> 00:01:06.692
We know more about each other
than me and my husband, and he
and his wife.

00:01:06.692 --> 00:01:11.863
But, it's inevitable that they
have some difficult and rocky
times.

00:01:11.863 --> 00:01:12.864
I'm sorry!

00:01:12.864 --> 00:01:14.074
Me too!

00:01:14.074 --> 00:01:18.578
Mitch, he's so charming and
likable, he doesn't really
realize the power and

00:01:18.578 --> 00:01:23.125
it's affect on other people. I
mean he does bad things, and I
think it's disconcerting. 

00:01:23.125 --> 00:01:25.585
But I love the fact that it's so
grey and complicated.

00:01:25.585 --> 00:01:29.715
He's a very flawed human being,
but he's a human being.

00:01:29.715 --> 00:01:32.301
You are my best friend, you are
like a part of me.

00:01:32.301 --> 00:01:33.510
Me too, honey.

00:01:33.510 --> 00:01:36.722
Reese Witherspoon:
Alex Levy has
been at The Morning Show for 17 years,

00:01:36.722 --> 00:01:38.932
Reese Witherspoon:
but her entire world has fallen
apart.

00:01:38.932 --> 00:01:41.893
Reese Witherspoon:
And she's grasping to get
control of her life again.

00:01:41.893 --> 00:01:45.772
I just need to be able to
control the narrative so that I
am not written out of it.

00:01:45.772 --> 00:01:51.236
My relevance is at stake here,
everything that I live for is
all in this show,

00:01:51.236 --> 00:01:53.238
and she's fighting for her life.

00:01:53.238 --> 00:01:55.407
I'm not closing without Carl's
approval.

00:01:55.407 --> 00:01:57.409
Well I'm sorry to hear that
because you're not getting it.

00:01:57.409 --> 00:01:58.410
(Music)

00:01:58.410 --> 00:02:00.954
So, Bradley, what is your story?

00:02:00.954 --> 00:02:02.039
I don't fit the mould.

00:02:02.039 --> 00:02:03.040
What mould is that?

00:02:03.040 --> 00:02:04.041
Any mould, really.

00:02:04.041 --> 00:02:08.670
Bradley Jackson comes in and
completely stirs the pot.

00:02:08.670 --> 00:02:12.424
She has a tendency to not think
before she speaks.

00:02:12.424 --> 00:02:14.718
Well you know how many jobs have
been lost in the last 10 years?
Huh?

00:02:14.718 --> 00:02:15.761
I don't know!

00:02:15.761 --> 00:02:16.762
Thousands!

00:02:16.762 --> 00:02:20.307
So when she gets the opportunity
to be on The Morning Show,

00:02:20.307 --> 00:02:22.309
Reese Witherspoon:
she's determined to sort of make
the best of that.

00:02:22.309 --> 00:02:23.894
We want to interview you.

00:02:23.894 --> 00:02:24.895
The Morning Show?

00:02:24.895 --> 00:02:26.897
Your words spoke to America.

00:02:26.897 --> 00:02:28.231
(Music)

00:02:28.231 --> 00:02:32.652
These characters go on a long
journey together in a very short
period of time.

00:02:32.652 --> 00:02:34.446
Mimi Leder:
How they get there is
fascinating.

00:02:34.446 --> 00:02:36.656
So you're a diehard reporter.

00:02:36.656 --> 00:02:38.033
The truth matters to me.

00:02:38.033 --> 00:02:41.953
The truth is what we are all
striving for.

00:02:41.953 --> 00:02:42.954
Yeah.

00:02:42.954 --> 00:02:47.793
Here's someone younger and who
has tapped into the fearlessness
in her quest for the truth.

00:02:47.793 --> 00:02:50.337
Jennifer Aniston:
What Bradley says resonates
within Alex,

00:02:50.337 --> 00:02:52.297
but she's also
terrified of it.

00:02:52.297 --> 00:02:56.301
These two complicated women in a
complicated work environment,

00:02:56.301 --> 00:03:01.139
Kerry Ehrin:
are gonna eventually collide and
it's a world that's often dark.

00:03:01.139 --> 00:03:04.601
Kerry Ehrin:
But also, there's definitely a
beating heart in it.

00:03:04.601 --> 00:03:05.977
And I think a hope.

00:03:05.977 --> 00:03:10.982
You all are so convinced that
you are the rightful owner of
all of the power that it doesn't

00:03:10.982 --> 00:03:14.444
even occur to you that someone
else could be in the driver's
seat.

00:03:14.444 --> 00:03:18.657
I think it's really powerful and
emotional.

00:03:18.657 --> 00:03:21.243
I gave up everything for this
show!

00:03:21.243 --> 00:03:23.370
Any chance of having a
normal life!

00:03:23.370 --> 00:03:24.371
(Music)

00:03:24.371 --> 00:03:25.997
I think it's really about a
reckoning.

00:03:25.997 --> 00:03:27.082
Just stay!

00:03:27.082 --> 00:03:29.126
Realizing that it's time for
change.

00:03:29.126 --> 00:03:36.341
(Music)

